<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea sells dollars at 865.00 won - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea sells dollars at 865.00 won - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea intervened in the interbank market in early Tuesday morning to slow the won's decline against the U.S. dollar, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the central bank sold dollars minutes after the local currency opened trading at 865.00 won per dollar, compared with Monday's closing rate of 864.90.</p>
<p>The bank refused to comment.  </p>
<p>The won rebounded to 860.10 soon after the intervention.</p>
<p>Dealers said demand for the U.S. unit remained high due to import settlements as the nation's export slump continues.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
